      "raw_answer": "```json\n{\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"get-order-authorization\",\n      \"title\": \"New GET /orders/<id> endpoint with owner-or-admin authorization\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The single added hunk introduces a new order-fetch endpoint. Its authorization behavior depends on three external pieces: the @require_auth decorator (which sets g.current_user), the is_owner_or_admin helper (the per-object ownership check mandated by security-policy.md \u00a73), and the Order model's user_id field that the check compares against. All of these are outside the diff but determine whether the endpoint correctly enforces 'owner or admin only' access, so they are grouped as the authorization context for this change.\",\n      \"hunks\": [\"app/routes/orders.py#0\"],\n      \"context\": [\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"require_auth\", \"start_line\": 55, \"end_line\": 66, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Decorator applied to get_order; sets g.current_user from the bearer token and returns 401 if absent. The endpoint's g.current_user reference depends on this.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/auth.py\", \"symbol\": \"is_owner_or_admin\", \"start_line\": 107, \"end_line\": 109, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"The ownership check used at line 65 of the new endpoint; returns True if user.id == owner_id or user.role == 'admin'. This is the core authorization gate for the endpoint.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/models.py\", \"symbol\": \"Order\", \"start_line\": 43, \"end_line\": 62, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"The Order model whose user_id field (line 47) is passed to is_owner_or_admin, and whose to_dict() (line 55) is returned to the client. The authorization check and data exposure both depend on this model.\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/users.py\", \"symbol\": \"get_user\", \"start_line\": 28, \"end_line\": 38, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Existing analogous endpoint (GET /users/<id>) that uses the same @require_auth + is_owner_or_admin pattern, providing the established authorization convention this new endpoint should follow.\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
